                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose where AI helps and where it hurts`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `The trap is treating “AI” as one decision. It is a <strong>portfolio</strong> of use cases with very different risk-and-value profiles. <strong>Targeting / bid optimisation</strong> is lower-risk, high-value. <strong>Autonomous content</strong> is high-value but high-risk — it is exactly what fabricated the “40%” claim that cost £1.2M and seven trust points. <strong>Personalised pricing</strong> is medium-value but high-risk: a customer who screenshots two prices for one serum is your next viral post. Plot each on value vs. brand-trust risk and make a first-cut <em>deploy / pilot / hold</em> call for each.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Deploy AI across the mix under constraint`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Now choose the <strong>autonomy level</strong> per use case — human-led with AI assist, AI-led with human approval, or fully autonomous — and split the fixed <strong>£4.0M</strong> across AI tooling, human oversight and brand-building. The configurations that cut CPA fastest — autonomous content, aggressive personalised pricing — are exactly those that most threaten the “honest beauty” equity. Tooling buys efficiency; oversight buys safety; <em>brand-building rebuilds the trust the incident destroyed</em>. Starve any one and you pay for it.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Write the human-oversight & brand-safety policy`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Design the governance that lets AI scale without another incident. Set the <strong>claim-substantiation gate</strong> (what must a human approve before content ships), a <strong>fairness check</strong> so the optimiser doesn't quietly exclude a core segment, a <strong>pricing-transparency</strong> rule, and an <strong>incident-response playbook</strong> for the next viral moment. Calibrate to risk: <em>strong where claims and fairness are at stake, light where they are not</em>. A policy that needs legal sign-off on every asset kills the speed advantage; a policy with no gate invites the next fabricated claim.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Commit, forecast & defend to the board`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Deliver the case to the CEO and the risk chair. Commit a two-quarter <strong>CPA trajectory</strong>, state your <strong>incident tolerance</strong>, and show how trust recovers from 64 back toward 71. The CEO presses for faster cuts; the risk chair presses on what stops the next viral screenshot. The trap is promising <em>both</em> maximum efficiency <em>and</em> zero risk — or sacrificing the brand to hit a CPA number that won't survive a second trust collapse. Efficiency and brand are complements, not substitutes. Make the trade-off explicit.`,

                    r1_frame_label:         `Is "adopt AI" one decision, or a portfolio of use cases with different risk?`,
                    r1_targeting_label:     `Targeting / bid optimisation — lower risk, high value. Your first-cut call:`,
