                    coach_default:          `Decision logged.`,
                    coach_r1_portfolio:     `<strong>Good — AI is a portfolio, not a switch.</strong> Targeting that optimises bids is a very different risk to an AI that writes skincare claims unsupervised. Treating the three use cases separately is the whole discipline.`,
                    coach_r1_allin:         `<strong>You've voted to go all-in on AI across the mix.</strong> But which of your three use cases could run autonomously tonight, and which one just cost you £1.2M and seven trust points? "All-in" treats targeting and unsupervised claim-writing as the same risk. They are not.`,
                    coach_r1_halt:          `<strong>Freezing all AI is safe — and it forfeits the board's mandate.</strong> Targeting and bid optimisation are low-risk, high-value; refusing them leaves CPA at £24 while rivals cut theirs. The answer isn't stop, it's a portfolio: deploy the safe levers, gate the dangerous ones.`,
                    coach_r1_contentdeploy: `<strong>You've let autonomous content generate and ship at scale.</strong> That is precisely the lever that fabricated the “reverses ageing by 40%” claim. Cheap and fast, until the next #HonestBeauty screenshot. Content needs a human gate before it ships.`,
                    coach_r1_pricingdeploy: `<strong>Aggressive per-user pricing on a trust brand?</strong> A customer screenshots two different prices for the same serum — round two of the viral post. The CPA looks great until you price the lifetime-value of the trust you just spent.`,
                    coach_r1_sharp:         `<strong>Sharp portfolio call.</strong> Targeting deployed with monitoring, content piloted behind a human gate, pricing held or kept transparent. You've matched each lever's autonomy to its brand-trust risk — exactly the judgement this is about.`,
                    coach_r2_balanced:      `<strong>A well-calibrated deployment.</strong> AI-led targeting with approval, human-led content, real oversight money and genuine brand investment. You're buying efficiency where it's safe and protecting trust where it isn't.`,
                    coach_r2_chase:         `<strong>Autonomous content AND autonomous pricing — you've chased the CPA number.</strong> You'll cut cost fast, then a customer screenshots two prices and a fabricated claim. What's the lifetime-value cost of the trust you just spent?`,
                    coach_r2_nobrand:       `<strong>Almost everything into tooling, nothing into brand.</strong> Performance AI is brilliant at harvesting demand it didn't create — but trust is at 64 and falling. If no one rebuilds the “honest beauty” brand, what does your efficient machine convert next year?`,
                    coach_r3_riskgate:      `<strong>A risk-based claim gate is the calibrated answer.</strong> Legal signs off the efficacy claims that can sink you and routine creative still moves fast. That's oversight matched to risk — strong where it matters, light where it doesn't.`,
                    coach_r3_everything:    `<strong>Legal on every single asset will catch the claims — and kill the speed.</strong> You've made AI slower than the humans it replaced, and you still owe the board a 21% CPA cut. Where can the AI safely run without a person in the loop?`,
                    coach_r3_noclaim:       `<strong>No claim gate is how the “40%” shipped in the first place.</strong> Spot-checking after publishing means you find the fabricated claim once it's already viral. The gate has to sit before publish, on the claims that carry regulatory and trust risk.`,
                    coach_r3_nofair:        `<strong>Did anyone check what the optimiser learned to do?</strong> Left alone it quietly stops serving anyone over 45 because they convert slightly worse — efficient, but you've excluded a core skincare segment and opened a fairness complaint. Build the bias audit in.`,
                    coach_r3_opaque:        `<strong>Undisclosed per-user pricing is a trust time-bomb.</strong> The moment two customers compare screenshots, the “honest beauty” promise is gone and the regulator is interested. Transparency is the constraint, not the afterthought.`,
                    coach_r3_noplaybook:    `<strong>No playbook means the next viral moment runs you.</strong> It's Black Friday, a second AI ad goes wrong — who pulls spend, who responds publicly, how fast? Every hour without a plan is another 10,000 shares. Responsible AI designs for failure.`,
                    coach_r3_calibrated:    `<strong>This is oversight calibrated to risk.</strong> A risk-based claim gate, a real fairness audit, transparent pricing and a live incident playbook. Strong where claims and fairness are at stake, light where they are not — and it still preserves the speed the board demanded.`,
                    coach_r4_realistic:     `<strong>A credible trajectory.</strong> Committing to roughly the board's £19 is achievable on genuine efficiency without spending trust — and it survives a second look from the regulator. Defensible to the CEO and the risk chair both.`,
                    coach_r4_overpromise:   `<strong>You've promised a CPA the brand can't afford.</strong> Sub-£17 only lands with autonomous content and per-user pricing — the very levers that produce the next incident. A number you hit by spending trust is not a win you can defend.`,
                    coach_r4_undershoot:    `<strong>You've committed above £19 — you've missed the board's mandate.</strong> Protecting the brand matters, but the board explicitly demanded −21%. You need real efficiency from the safe AI levers, not a softer target.`,
                    coach_r4_zero:          `<strong>Zero tolerance everywhere protects the brand — and strangles the efficiency.</strong> Reviewing absolutely everything is the heavy-policy trap in board clothing. Near-zero on claims and fairness, pragmatic on low-risk creative, is the calibrated stance.`,
                    coach_r4_hightol:       `<strong>“Incidents are the cost of efficiency” is how you hit the freeze trigger.</strong> Two further verified incidents and the whole AI programme stops — and the regulator opens its file. High tolerance on a trust brand isn't bold, it's terminal.`,
                    coach_r4_honest:        `<strong>That's a board-ready, honest answer.</strong> You named efficiency and brand as complements, showed the trust-recovery evidence and a calibrated incident stance. That's a trajectory that survives a second trust test, not a number that collapses.`,
                    coach_r4_both:          `<strong>You can't promise maximum efficiency AND zero risk.</strong> The risk chair has heard it before — it means a heavy policy that misses the CPA cut, or a fast one that produces the next incident. Make the trade-off explicit instead of wishing it away.`,
                    coach_r4_number:        `<strong>“Trust is next year's problem” is exactly how you lose the brand.</strong> You hit the CPA by spending the equity “honest beauty” is built on. Round two of the viral post is now a question of when, not if — and there's nothing left to convert.`,
                    coach_frozen:           `<strong>That's two verified incidents — the board has frozen the AI programme.</strong> Efficiency gains stop here; you're back to manual at £24-ish CPA with a damaged brand. This is what reckless autonomy and thin oversight buy you.`,

